==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
the first Zombie Outbreak is relatively straightforward, with Zoge and Zir Zeal being the Zombies for this stage. It can be completed by using meatshields to not let Zir Zeal use [[Freeze]] on important units, and using strong Anti-Zombie units like [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Gardener]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu]]. The [[Imperator Sael|Imperator Saels]] can be defeated by units like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer]] or [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Wheel]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Spawn as many fast moving meatshields as you can early on so you can force The Thrillerz to burrow. Then, summon something to kill them as you prepare for the seals to spawn.

Once the enemy base reaches 99%, a pair of seals will spawn, Zir Zeal burrows immediately get behind your front line. Perfect cat cannon timing can help with the first one but the second Zir spawns too quickly for your cannon to recharge. Be prepared with back up zombie killers to keep the Zir Zeal and his long burrow away from your cat base.

Some anti-alien units for Imperator Sael can be helpful as his slow is not to be underestimated. Similarly, the freeze effect from Zir Zeal can destroy your front line so any zombie CC is a huge boost.

The biggest problem with this stage is money, Thrillerz give very little cash and you can't stall forever. Having cheap units that deal good damage is essential and having 4 meatshields is recommended.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Using specialized meatshields like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] will make fighting Angelic Gories and Zombie threats easier. Since Li'l Zyclones have a lot of health but low damage, it allows you to use long-range units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and use them as a stepping stone to safely attack enemies. It's recommended to have [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to prevent Zombies enemies from cutting off your meatshield flow.

